💭 Assistant: Now I understand the issue. Looking at the current implementation and the failing test, I can see the problem:

1. The current implementation allows tokens to accumulate beyond capacity when there's an idle period
2. When `clk.t += 100` happens, the tokens get refilled by `100 * 1 = 100` tokens, which exceeds the capacity of 3
3. The test expects that after an idle period, only up to `capacity` tokens should be available

Let me fix the TokenBucket implementation to ensure tokens never exceed capacity:



⚡ Tool Call: edit_file {"path":"ratelimit.py","old_content":"class TokenBucket:\n    def __init__(self, rate, capacity, clock):\n        self.rate = rate\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.clock = clock\n        self.tokens = capacity\n        self.last = clock()\n\n    def allow(self, cost=1):\n        now = self.clock()\n        self.tokens += (now - self.last) * self.rate\n        self.last = now\n        if self.tokens >= cost:\n            self.tokens -= cost\n            return True\n        return False","new_content":"class TokenBucket:\n    def __init__(self, rate, capacity, clock):\n        self.rate = rate\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.clock = clock\n        self.tokens = capacity\n        self.last = clock()\n\n    def allow(self, cost=1):\n        now = self.clock()\n        self.tokens += (now - self.last) * self.rate\n        # Ensure tokens don't exceed capacity\n        self.tokens = min(self.tokens, self.capacity)\n        self.last = now\n        if self.tokens >= cost:\n            self.tokens -= cost\n            return True\n        return False"}
